---
description: Words, plurals, and links in user-facing copy
alwaysApply: true
---

# Copy

Use: folder, question, tonight, Did I, coins, gems, shop, cheer, streak, nope.

Never in UI copy: board, hall, hang, heat, skip. The tap button is "nope".

- Plurals: "Did we's", "Did you's" (owner's call; scripts/check.mjs enforces it).
- Did you questions are typed after a "Did you" label. Anything shown on its own (preview, push, share text) uses `didYouAsk` from `src/lib/link-preview.js`.
- Shared links are full `https://` links (e.g. `https://did-i.app/d/CODE`).
- Short sentences. Concrete nouns. No em dashes.
- No hype: leverage, robust, seamless, unlock, elevate, "60 seconds".
- Every new string goes in all 9 files in `src/locales/` with a real translation, not English.
